// QA2 (AC-2, independent re-derivation) — the two swagger failure modes the
// coder's tests do NOT reach:
//  1. spec DTO ACCURACY: the served openapi.json definitions reference the
//     handler DTOs' real property names (the R-3 drift catcher at the DTO
//     level). The coder only counts path keys + operationIds — a DTO that lost
//     a field in the spec would pass.
//  2. served == committed bytes: the serve path is a pure embed passthrough
//     (no runtime mutation). The coder never compares served vs the committed
//     file on disk.
//
// Also verifies the R-01 cleanup landed in the spec: api.libraryResponse is
// ABSENT and POST /libraries refs the single api.libraryDTO.
//
// Existing coverage (do not re-prove): web_test.go::TestHandler_Swagger +
// TestHandler_SwaggerNotFallback (yaml/json 200 + content-types + not-fallback
// + /docs loads); integration_web_test.go::ac2_swagger (5 path keys + 6
// operationIds + /docs 200 + public).
